{"name":"Sandcastle","hex":"#e5d7c4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sandcastle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sculpture made of sand and resembling a miniature castle; typically, but not always, made for fun by a child on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sandcastle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sandcastle (software)","blocks":[{"text":"Sandcastle is a documentation generator from Microsoft. It automatically produces MSDN-style code documentation out of reflection information of .NET assemblies and XML documentation comments found in the source code of these assemblies. It can also be used to produce user documentation from Microsoft Assistance Markup Language (MAML) with the same look and feel as reference documentation."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandcastle_(software)","wikidata":"Q4049040"},{"title":"Sandcastle (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Sandcastle is a 2011 French-language graphic novel published by Atrabile, written by Pierre Oscar Lévy from France and drawn by Frederik Peeters from Switzerland. Nora Mahony translated the work into English, with that version released in 2013. SelfMadeHero published the English version."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandcastle_(comics)","wikidata":"Q108339209"},{"title":"Sand art and play","blocks":[{"text":"Sand art is the practice of modelling sand into an artistic form, such as sand brushing, sand sculpting, sand painting, or creating sand bottles. A sandcastle is a type of sand sculpture resembling a miniature building, often a castle. The drip castle variation uses wet sand that is dribbled down to form organic shapes before the sand dries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Sand_art_of_Ratha_Yatra_by_Sudarsan_Pattnaik.jpg/330px-Sand_art_of_Ratha_Yatra_by_Sudarsan_Pattnaik.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand_art_and_play","w